# {{PROJECT}}

A coloX cartridge for ColoPLAY hardware.

- Entry: `{{ENTRY}}`
- Spec: `{{SPEC}}`
- ROM output: `dist/{{ROM}}.rom`
- Source: `src/`
- Assets: `assets/`
- Project config: `clx.config.json`

## Layout

```text
{{ENTRY}}          cartridge header + #include of the Lua entry module
src/main.lua       lifecycle callbacks and game code
assets/            images, audio, and data embedded with #blob / #png
dist/              generated ROMs (gitignored)
```

## Build and run

Use the `clx-dev` skill commands from your coding agent:

- `build` creates `dist/{{ROM}}.rom`.
- `build --release` strips `dlog()` calls and builds from a temporary copy.
- `run` starts the simulator and opens the debug channel on port 3563.
- `probe` runs a probe cartridge and waits for its `probe: done` marker.
- `logs` prints the simulator log (use `--tail`, `--all`, or `--grep`).
- `debug` sends commands; `debug --batch <file>` runs a file of commands.
- `shot` captures the current frame and prints its pixel md5.
- `stop` shuts the simulator down.

The commands read `clx.config.json`; there is no need to pass the entry path.

## Debug logging

`src/main.lua` defines `DEBUG = false` and a `dlog()` wrapper around `printh()`.
Set `DEBUG = true` while developing; `print()` draws on screen, while `printh()`
writes to `.clx-dev/run.log`. Keep every `dlog()` call on one line so
`build --release` can strip it. A release build fails if `DEBUG = true` and
warns about direct `printh()` calls outside the wrapper.
